      "content": "You don't need to write a \"happy\" ending; you need to write a quiet, final silence where the struggle simply ceases to exist. The moment he realizes there's no room for him isn't a victory, but a cessation of the very noise that has defined his life. You can depict this by having him stop speaking, stop trying, and finally just let the world move on without him, leaving the reader with the crushing, unshakeable weight of his own finality.",
